From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Linux desktop branding (Micromium)

- Points the .desktop file, icons and app ID at Micromium branding
- Keeps Google API keys empty by default on Linux builds

Rebased against Chromium 153.0.8010.27 (branch 1681091).

--- a/chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING
+++ b/chrome/app/theme/chromium/BRANDING
@@ -8,3 +8,4 @@
 MAC_BUNDLE_ID=org.chromium.Chromium
 MAC_CREATOR_CODE=Cr24
+MICROMIUM_APP_ID=micromium.browser.stable
 MAC_TEAM_ID=
--- a/chrome/browser/shell_integration_linux.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/shell_integration_linux.cc
@@ -6,3 +6,5 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/shell_integration_linux.h"
 
+// Micromium (Linux): register micromium-browser.desktop; no Google update
+// ping unless the user opts in (see linux/default_flags.json).
 #include <fcntl.h>
